course: dictionary
lesson: 8379
title: Royalty: more than kings and queens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «A royalty is money paid to music makers when their work is used.» Here the words money and paid tell you that royalty means a payment, not a king or queen.
explain: In a history book, royalty means the royal family: kings, queens, princes and princesses. In a story about a band, the same word can mean money. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases use royalty in a special way. If someone is treated like royalty, they get great respect and special care. This is a comparison, not a sentence about real kings and queens. Look for words like like and treated, which show the phrase is describing how someone is treated.
fact: Royalty can mean kings, queens, princes, princesses and their families.
fact: Royalty can also mean the state of being royal.
fact: Royalties are payments made to writers, musicians or inventors each time their work is sold or used.
fact: «A royalty is money paid to music makers when their work is used.»
fact: «Treated like royalty» means given great respect and special care.
exercise: «A royalty is money paid to music makers when their work is used.» What is a royalty here? | *Money paid to music makers when their work is used | A prize given to the best school choir | A song played loudly at a party | A ring worn by queens at a royal wedding
exercise: In a history lesson, what does royalty mean? | A type of cold weather | Payments made to inventors | *The royal family: kings, queens, princes and princesses | Music makers and their songs
exercise: A writer gets royalties from book sales. What are royalties? | *Payments to the writer each time the book is sold or used | Money the shop keeps for itself | Prizes given by the school library | A free copy of the book for every reader
test: «The band was treated like royalty at the party.» What does treated like royalty suggest? | Sent home early | Asked to pay for everything | Forgotten by everyone | *Given great respect and special care
test: Which word means the payments made to a writer each time a book is sold? | Loyalty | *Royalties | Regal | Royal
exam: Which answer shows the most meanings of royalty? | Only money paid to writers and musicians | Only kings and queens | *Kings, queens and their families, the state of being royal, and money paid to writers and musicians | Only the state of being rich
